IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc32-nif-xxi1-transition.l4 -- AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE: the transitional provisions of 2024, c. 33, ss 7 to 13 (applications made to the Minister of Justice under the old Part XXI.1,
-- and what happens to them when the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission starts), from the end of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (lines 19651-19690 of the text).
-- Part ccc32, layer 1. Every name here begins with `2024 c 33 s N`. These are the rules for the person whose application is pending with the Minister: who asks them, what happens if they consent, refuse or stay silent.
-- A duty with no period in the text (section 8: the Minister "must ask") is a regulative rule WITHOUT a WITHIN, with a decision twin (a DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable binary).
-- How a result reads, the naming rule and the rule for days the text leaves open: see the head of ccc32-related-1.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `2024, c. 33, s. 7 -- definitions for this section and sections 8 to 13`

-- 7 The following definitions apply in this section and sections 8 to 13. A scope limit with no "only": outside it NOT COVERED.
-- src:19652 | Definitions
-- src:19653 | 7 The following definitions apply in this section and sections 8 to 13.
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 (src:19652-19653)
GIVEN `the number of the section of 2024, c. 33` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 7 the definitions apply in the section` MEANS
    IF `the number of the section of 2024, c. 33` EQUALS 7 OR (`the number of the section of 2024, c. 33` AT LEAST 8 AND `the number of the section of 2024, c. 33` AT MOST 13)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following definitions apply in this section and sections 8 to 13"

-- applicant means the person who is the subject of the finding or verdict in question or their representative.
-- src:19654 | applicant means the person who is the subject of the finding or verdict in question or their representative. (demandeur)
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "applicant" (src:19654)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of the finding or verdict in question or their representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 7 "applicant"` MEANS
    IF `the person is the subject of the finding or verdict in question or their representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "applicant means the person who is the subject of the finding or verdict in question or their representative"

-- commencement day means the day on which section 3 comes into force. A defined term that points at a day: the function returns the day (section 3's day is not in the sources: an input).
-- src:19655 | commencement day means the day on which section 3 comes into force. (date de référence)
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "commencement day" (src:19655)
GIVEN `the day on which section 3 of 2024, c. 33 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`2024 c 33 s 7 "commencement day"` MEANS `the day on which section 3 of 2024, c. 33 comes into force`

-- Commission means the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) of the Criminal Code.
-- src:19656 | Commission means the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) of the Criminal Code. (Commission)
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "Commission" (src:19656)
GIVEN `the body is the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 7 "Commission"` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) of the Criminal Code`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Commission means the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) of the Criminal Code"

-- Minister means the Minister of Justice.
-- src:19657 | Minister means the Minister of Justice. (ministre)
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "Minister" (src:19657)
GIVEN `the person is the Minister of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 7 "Minister"` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Minister of Justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Minister means the Minister of Justice"

-- new scheme means Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code as it reads on or after the commencement day.
-- src:19658 | new scheme means Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code as it reads on or after the commencement day. (nouveau régime)
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "new scheme" (src:19658)
GIVEN `the text is Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day as of which the text is read` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 3 of 2024, c. 33 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 7 "new scheme"` MEANS
    IF `the text is Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code` AND `the day as of which the text is read` AT LEAST `the day on which section 3 of 2024, c. 33 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "new scheme means Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code as it reads on or after the commencement day"

-- old scheme means Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code and the Regulations Respecting Applications for Ministerial Review -- Miscarriages of Justice as they read immediately before the commencement day.
-- "Immediately before" is read as the text in force on the day before the commencement day (fork F10).
-- src:19659 | old scheme means Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code and the Regulations Respecting Applications for Ministerial Review — Miscarriages of Justice as they read immediately before the commencement day. (ancien régime)
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "old scheme" (src:19659)
DECLARE `2024 c 33 s 7 text of the old scheme` IS ONE OF
    `2024 c 33 s 7 Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code`
    `2024 c 33 s 7 the Regulations Respecting Applications for Ministerial Review — Miscarriages of Justice`
    `2024 c 33 s 7 another text`

@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 7 "old scheme" (src:19659)
GIVEN text IS A `2024 c 33 s 7 text of the old scheme`
      `the day as of which the text is read` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 3 of 2024, c. 33 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 7 "old scheme"` MEANS
    IF text EQUALS `2024 c 33 s 7 another text`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "old scheme means Part XXI.1 of the Criminal Code and the Regulations Respecting Applications for Ministerial Review"
    ELSE IF `the day as of which the text is read` EQUALS (`the day on which section 3 of 2024, c. 33 comes into force` MINUS 1)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as they read immediately before the commencement day"

§ `2024, c. 33, ss. 8 to 13 -- what happens to an application made to the Minister under the old scheme`

-- 8 If an application was made under the old scheme and the Minister has not, before the commencement day, made a decision under subsection 696.3(3) of the Criminal Code, as it read immediately before that day,
-- the Minister must ask the applicant whether they consent to having the application transferred to the Commission to be dealt with in accordance with the new scheme. No period is stated: no WITHIN.
-- src:19662 | Duty of Minister
-- src:19663 | 8 If an application was made under the old scheme and the Minister has not, before the commencement day, made a decision under subsection 696.3(3) of the Criminal Code, as it read immediately before that day, the Minister must ask the applicant whether they consent to having the application transferred to the Commission to be dealt with in accordance with the new scheme.
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 8 (src:19662-19663)
DECLARE `2024 c 33 s 8 act` IS ONE OF
    `2024 c 33 s 8 ask the applicant whether they consent to having the application transferred to the Commission to be dealt with in accordance with the new scheme`

@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 8 (src:19662-19663)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2024 c 33 s 8 act`
`2024 c 33 s 8 the Minister must ask the applicant whether they consent to the transfer` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister of Justice`
    MUST `2024 c 33 s 8 ask the applicant whether they consent to having the application transferred to the Commission to be dealt with in accordance with the new scheme`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister of Justice` BECAUSE "the Minister did not ask the applicant whether they consent to having the application transferred to the Commission"

@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 8 (src:19662-19663)
GIVEN `the application was made under the old scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has not, before the commencement day, made a decision under subsection 696.3(3) of the Criminal Code, as it read immediately before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 8 the Minister owes the duty to ask the applicant whether they consent to the transfer` MEANS
    IF `the application was made under the old scheme` AND `the Minister has not, before the commencement day, made a decision under subsection 696.3(3) of the Criminal Code, as it read immediately before that day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application was made under the old scheme and the Minister has not, before the commencement day, made a decision under subsection 696.3(3) of the Criminal Code"

-- 9 If the applicant gives, within the time limit fixed by the Minister, written consent to transfer the application, the application is deemed to have been made to the Commission under the new scheme and the Minister is authorized
-- to disclose to the Commission all information pertaining to the application that is under the Minister's control. A failed "if" is the text's no within the provision (marginal reading).
-- src:19666 | Consent within deadline
-- src:19667 | 9 If the applicant gives, within the time limit fixed by the Minister, written consent to transfer the application, the application is deemed to have been made to the Commission under the new scheme and the Minister is authorized to disclose to the Commission all information pertaining to the application that is under the Minister’s control.
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 9 (src:19666-19667)
GIVEN `the consent to transfer the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the applicant gives the consent` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the time limit fixed by the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 9 the application is deemed to have been made to the Commission under the new scheme` MEANS
    IF `the consent to transfer the application is in writing` AND `the day the applicant gives the consent` AT MOST `the last day of the time limit fixed by the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the applicant gives, within the time limit fixed by the Minister, written consent to transfer the application"

@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 9 (src:19666-19667)
GIVEN `the consent to transfer the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the applicant gives the consent` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the time limit fixed by the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- Named for a power (the Minister "is authorized"): when the "If" gate fails the grant is limited by its own wording, so NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading, a failed "if" as the text's no, is fork F21 in NOTES.md).
`2024 c 33 s 9 the Minister is authorized to disclose to the Commission all information pertaining to the application that is under the Minister’s control` MEANS
    IF `the consent to transfer the application is in writing` AND `the day the applicant gives the consent` AT MOST `the last day of the time limit fixed by the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the applicant gives, within the time limit fixed by the Minister, written consent to transfer the application"

-- 10 (1) If the applicant, within the time limit fixed by the Minister, does not reply in writing to the Minister or gives a written refusal of consent to transfer the application, subsection (2) or (3) applies.
-- src:19670 | No consent
-- src:19671 | 10 (1) If the applicant, within the time limit fixed by the Minister, does not reply in writing to the Minister or gives a written refusal of consent to transfer the application, subsection (2) or (3) applies.
