-- (2) If, before the commencement day, the Minister completed the preliminary assessment of the application required under paragraph 3(b) of the Regulations, the old scheme continues to apply in respect of the application.
-- (2) is reached through subsection (1): where (1) did not apply the answer is NOT COVERED.
-- src:19672 | Preliminary assessment completed
-- src:19673 | (2) If, before the commencement day, the Minister completed the preliminary assessment of the application required under paragraph 3(b) of the Regulations Respecting Applications for Ministerial Review — Miscarriages of Justice, the old scheme continues to apply in respect of the application.
@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 10(2) (src:19672-19673)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection 10(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Minister completed the preliminary assessment of the application required under paragraph 3(b) of the Regulations before the commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 10(2) the old scheme continues to apply in respect of the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the answer of subsection 10(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subsection (2) or (3) applies" is what subsection (1) says when it applies
        IF `the Minister completed the preliminary assessment of the application required under paragraph 3(b) of the Regulations before the commencement day` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, before the commencement day, the Minister completed the preliminary assessment of the application required under paragraph 3(b) of the Regulations Respecting Applications for Ministerial Review — Miscarriages of Justice"

