GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2024 c 33 s 10(3) the application is deemed not to have been made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the answer of subsection 10(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subsection (2) or (3) applies" is what subsection (1) says when it applies
        IF `the Minister did not complete the preliminary assessment before the commencement day` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Minister did not complete the preliminary assessment before the commencement day"

@ref 2024, c. 33, s. 10(3) (src:19674-19675)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection 10(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Minister did not complete the preliminary assessment before the commencement day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- Named for a power (the applicant "may apply"): when the "If" gate fails the grant is limited by its own wording, so NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading is fork F23 in NOTES.md).
`2024 c 33 s 10(3) the applicant may apply to the Commission under the new scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the answer of subsection 10(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subsection (2) or (3) applies" is what subsection (1) says when it applies
        IF `the Minister did not complete the preliminary assessment before the commencement day` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Minister did not complete the preliminary assessment before the commencement day"

-- 11 An application is deemed to have been made to the Commission under the new scheme and the Minister is authorized to disclose all information pertaining to it if (a) the applicant gives, after the time limit fixed by the Minister, written consent to transfer the application;
-- (b) the Minister completed the preliminary assessment before the commencement day; and (c) the Minister receives the consent before having made, under subsection 10(2) of this Act, a decision under subsection 696.3(3), as it read immediately before the commencement day.
